  data: {
    LLM: 'Bid on strong hands: aces, 10s, 5s (point cards), and long or void suits. Unbalanced distribution (long suits, at least one void) is desirable. Make your bid to score it; fail and your side loses the bid amount.\n\nTrack important cards (point cards and trumps) and which have been played. Remember opponentsâ€™ holes (voids). When your partner is winning a trick, throw them point cards to maximise team score.\n\nBidding: identify hands with aces, high cards, and sequences. Defence: try to force the bidder to lose point cards or trump. Communication through card play (leading high to show strength, etc.).',
